easywall (2.21.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New: blocked traffic is a page. The ten log switches send what they refuse
    to an NFLOG group (12227 by default, [packet_log] nflog_group), and
    easywall-core decodes each packet's headers into a typed entry kept in a
    ring of 20000. /blocked filters them by source, destination, port,
    protocol, rule and interface, with a drill-down and a live tail.
  * New: three actions on every row — whitelist the source, blacklist the
    source, open the port. They stage and never apply, and they refuse, with
    the reason, anything that would stop a new connection from the address
    the operator is signed in from, or from the trusted proxy in front.
  * Changed: journalctl -k no longer shows easywall's log lines on a host where
    the core binds its group. If the group cannot be bound — ulogd2 holds it,
    or the process lacks CAP_NET_ADMIN — the core says so at start, the page
    says so, and logging falls back to the kernel log, so an apply never fails
    because of it. With easywall-core stopped, logged packets are discarded.
  * Security: the optional spill file (persist = true, off by default) holds IP
    addresses, is 0600 root, rewrites itself once it holds more than twice the
    ring, and is never handed to logrotate. Nothing leaves the host.
  * New dependency: github.com/florianl/go-nflog/v2 v2.3.0 (MIT); its own
    dependencies were already in the module graph.

