easywall (2.20.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: the start-up log promised an acceptance window that was switched off.
    On a host nothing had ever been applied to, the restore summary said the
    first apply had the acceptance window to undo it, whether or not one was
    configured — a sentence that reads as a safety net and is not one. The
    promise now drops that clause where no window exists, start-up warns once
    when the window is off, and `easywall-core status` says so too.
  * Fix: health called an unprovable selftest a missing one. Inside a container
    there is no CAP_SYS_ADMIN, so the proof cannot be taken; the line said
    "never recorded", which reads as a failure somebody should chase. It now
    says the proof is unavailable there, probed from the process's own
    capabilities and failing open.
  * Fix: a Docker container could publish a port that no rule covered, and
    nothing said so. Every apply now names each published port with no matching
    rule, decoded from Docker's own DNAT rules over netlink and filtered to
    targets inside the bridges it detects. It names the port the forward chain
    will see: a remapped publish is DNAT'd before that chain, so `-p 8080:80`
    needs a rule for 80 and the line says both numbers. A forwarded rule that
    names sources does not silence the warning for a container outside them.
  * Docs: how a service published on a bridge gateway is reached, why it needs
    a forwarded rule of its own, and how to prove a silent UDP service is
    reachable by reading the packet counters rather than waiting for a reply.

